        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this superb three-bedroom, two-bathroom semi-detached family home to the market in the highly sought-after and mature location of Hillcrest Park, Glasnevin, Dublin 11. No. 128 is ideally positioned within a quiet cul-de-sac and offers bright, spacious and well-proportioned accommodation extending to approximately c.114 sq.m, together with a large front driveway, side access and a magnificent south-west facing rear garden.\n\nThis wonderful family home has been extremely well maintained over the years and is sure to appeal to first-time buyers, growing families and those seeking to trade up in one of Dublin's most established residential locations.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance porch leading into a welcoming hallway with understairs storage. To the front lies a bright and spacious living room, while the hallway also leads to a separate dining room boasting a solid fuel stove, creating an ideal setting for family gatherings and entertaining. A downstairs Utility is conveniently located off the hallway, while to the rear a large kitchen extension provides an abundance of dining and living space and overlooks the impressive south-west facing rear garden, guest bathroom completes the ground floor.\n\nThe rear garden offers excellent privacy and is the perfect space for outdoor dining, entertaining and family enjoyment. A garden shed with electricity provides superb additional storage or potential for a home office, workshop or hobby space. The property also benefits from side access, gas fired central heating, double glazed windows throughout and an alarm system.\n\nUpstairs comprises a family bathroom, a generous master bedroom with built-in wardrobes, a spacious double bedroom also with built-in wardrobes and an additional single bedroom.\n\nHillcrest Park is within easy reach of a host of local shops, cafés, restaurants, takeaways, supermarkets, pharmacies and everyday conveniences, with Glasnevin Village and the surrounding areas offering everything needed for day-to-day living. Families are particularly well catered for with a wide selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools nearby, while Dublin City University, the National Botanic Gardens, Albert College Park, Griffith Park and a number of local sporting and recreational facilities are all within easy reach. The area is exceptionally well serviced by public transport, with several local bus stops within a short walk of the property providing regular routes towards Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas, while further bus routes are available along the nearby main roads. The property also offers excellent connectivity for commuters with easy access to the M50 and M1 motorways, Dublin Airport and Dublin City Centre further adds to the convenience of this superb family location.\n\nContact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 0861985247 or 015411455 to arrange a viewing or register your interest.\n\nKey Features:\n• BER C\n• c.114 sq.m\n• 3 bedroom / 2 bathroom semi-detached family home\n• Built 1969\n• Quiet cul-de-sac location\n• Large front driveway with ample off-street parking\n• Side access\n• Entrance porch\n• Bright living room with feature gas fireplace\n• Separate dining room with solid fuel stove\n• Large kitchen extension to the rear\n• Downstairs bathroom\n• Understairs storage\n• South-west facing rear garden\n• Garden shed with electricity\n• Gas fired central heating\n• Double glazed windows throughout\n• Alarmed\n• Master bedroom with built-in wardrobes\n• Double bedroom with built-in wardrobes\n• Single bedroom\n• Family bathroom upstairs\n• Mature and highly sought-after residential location\n• Excellent transport links\n• Close to DCU, Bon Secours Hospital and Glasnevin Village\n• Easy access to M50, M1 and Dublin Airport\n• Ideal for first-time buyers and growing families"
      },
